From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: align fwnode PCS count and parse API

Use the separate PCS reference counter to set num_possible_pcs and pass the
array capacity by value to the parser. The generic PCS provider now returns
the available count rather than updating a count pointer, and rejects a NULL
output array. Keep the existing Airoha PCS modes and topology unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Index: linux-6.18.55/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
===================================================================
--- linux-6.18.55.orig/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-09 19:28:46.671134386 -0700
+++ linux-6.18.55/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-09 19:29:07.424620418 -0700
@@ -3828,7 +3828,7 @@
 	struct device *dev = config->dev;
 
 	return fwnode_phylink_pcs_parse(dev_fwnode(dev), available_pcs,
-					&num_possible_pcs);
+					num_possible_pcs);
 }
 
 static int airoha_setup_phylink(struct net_device *netdev)
@@ -3866,10 +3866,8 @@
 					   MAC_10 | MAC_100 | MAC_1000 |
 					   MAC_2500FD | MAC_5000FD | MAC_10000FD;
 
-		err = fwnode_phylink_pcs_parse(dev_fwnode(config->dev), NULL,
-					       &dev->phylink_config.num_available_pcs);
-		if (err)
-			return err;
+		config->num_possible_pcs =
+			fwnode_phylink_pcs_count(dev_fwnode(config->dev));
 
 		config->fill_available_pcs = airoha_fill_available_pcs;
 
